Subject: [PATCH 22/38] fs: sharedfs: one device per export, mounted by tag

A guest may carry several exports: the project tree and the host's
configuration directory, for instance. Each is its own virtio device
with its own index, window and queues, and carries a tag NUL-padded at
the start of its configuration space, laid out as virtio-fs lays out
its tag. The driver keeps the bound sessions in a list keyed by tag,
refuses a second device with the same tag, and a mount names the tag as
its source: `mount -t sharedfs config /home/user/.config`.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SKmspe5nVbuvzdvYZa9UhW
